  "description": "The twelve projections no chart in the corpus had drawn, each given the same graticule and the same four cities so the differences between them are the only thing on screen. The three conics take their parallels from the specification, the azimuthals and the gnomonic clip to a cap around their centre, the orthographic shows only the hemisphere facing the reader, and the transverse Mercator is the ordinary one turned on its side. Nothing here is decorative: a projection is a pair of trigonometric formulas and a clip, and a wrong sign in either draws a plausible-looking map of somewhere else.",
